# 9. Relationship to Other GPL Business Units

## 9.1 Managed Services vs Software Services

Managed Services focuses on the ongoing stability, support, and operational state of the technology environment.

Software Services focuses on the software and workflow layer, including implementation, customization, integrations, automation, and production tooling.

A useful distinction is:

* Managed Services supports the environment in which production operates.
* Software Services improves the software workflows operating inside that environment.

Avoid turning Managed Services articles into discussions of custom application development, workflow automation, or production tracking configuration unless those subjects are directly relevant to an infrastructure or support issue.

## 9.2 Managed Services vs Security & Compliance

Managed Services and Security & Compliance may interact with the same technology environment, but they address different responsibilities.

Managed Services focuses primarily on ongoing infrastructure support, operational continuity, lifecycle, and service ownership.

Security & Compliance focuses on risk reduction, content protection, identity and access governance, security controls, compliance frameworks, and audit readiness.

A Managed Services article may discuss access, security, or risk when those issues affect day-to-day operations, but security governance should not become the central subject unless the article belongs to the Security & Compliance business unit.

## 9.3 Managed Services vs Consulting

Consulting is primarily strategic and advisory.

Managed Services is ongoing and operational.

Consulting may help an organization decide how an environment should evolve. Managed Services helps support the environment as it operates and changes over time.

## 9.4 Managed Services vs VFXNOW

VFXNOW provides production-ready hardware and compute resources.

Managed Services focuses on the ongoing operational environment around the technology.

VFXNOW is primarily about access to the hardware required to execute production work. Managed Services is about keeping the broader technology environment supportable and aligned with production needs.

