# 14. Editorial Boundaries

Managed Services content should not become:

* generic advice about outsourcing IT
* “benefits of an MSP” content
* basic explanations of why downtime is bad
* introductory education about production environments
* long lists of infrastructure technologies
* generic cost-savings arguments
* security articles presented as Managed Services
* Software Services topics presented as infrastructure support
* service catalogs disguised as editorial content

Avoid proving GPL's industry knowledge through terminology.

The argument itself should demonstrate that the writer understands the environment.

